  "summary": "The Coralville (Iowa) City Council voted 3-1 to cancel its contract with Flock Safety and remove its ALPR cameras, after the Iowa Attorney General's Office flagged the city's use policy for limiting camera use for immigration enforcement in violation of state law. Rather than amend the policy, the council opted to remove the cameras, though the city remains liable for the remainder of the $36,000 two-year contract through July 2027.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "The Coralville City Council voted 3-1 in favor of canceling its contract with Flock Safety and removing the city's automatic license plate reader cameras in the next few days.",
      "paragraph_idx": 17
    },
    {
      "quote": "Earlier this month, the Iowa Attorney General's Office flagged the city's policy that limited the use of the cameras for immigration enforcement.",
      "paragraph_idx": 18
    },
    {
      "quote": "The Attorney General's Office complaint said the policy violated state law \u2014 Section 427.4.1(d) from policy 427 \u2014 when the policy stated Flock cameras may not be used \"solely for immigration purposes.\"",
      "paragraph_idx": 30
    }
  ],
